1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:01,770
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,770 --> 00:00:03,610
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:05,080
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:07,150 --> 00:00:08,280
(Episode 32)

5
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:15,220
Please stop.
You've had too much to drink.

6
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:17,820
Let go.

7
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:33,470
What are you two doing?

8
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:44,880
Well, the CEO wanted something.

9
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:48,790
I thought you had work to do.

10
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,920
Why are you drinking again?

11
00:00:58,430 --> 00:01:01,100
Can I help you with anything, ma'am?

12
00:01:02,900 --> 00:01:04,440
No, nothing.

13
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:07,010
Okay, then please get some rest.

14
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:28,730
What is it, Mom?

15
00:01:29,630 --> 00:01:31,230
Is it still not time?

16
00:01:31,530 --> 00:01:34,130
Is the nice lady not coming today?

17
00:01:34,630 --> 00:01:36,970
She will. Let's just be patient.

18
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,040
Okay.

19
00:01:42,410 --> 00:01:44,240
Hey, it's the nice lady.

20
00:01:45,010 --> 00:01:47,950
- Did you run here?
- Sorry. I kept you waiting, right?

21
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:49,710
The bus was late.

22
00:01:49,950 --> 00:01:51,120
It's fine.

23
00:01:51,180 --> 00:01:55,520
Mr. Seok Jin, move.
Nice lady, sit right here.

24
00:01:59,660 --> 00:02:02,260
- Have you been well?
- Yes, I've been well.

25
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:04,800
Here.

26
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,030
Did you do all of this yourself?

27
00:02:08,300 --> 00:02:10,270
Yes, this was all me.

28
00:02:10,700 --> 00:02:11,870
Didn't I do a good job?

29
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:15,770
Yes, it's amazing.
I love how colorful it is.

30
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:18,610
This belongs in a frame.

31
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,110
Really?

32
00:02:20,580 --> 00:02:24,620
Then I'll frame this...

33
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:26,280
and give it to you as a gift.

34
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:31,260
I'm going to hang it on my door
so I see it every day.

35
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:34,130
Wait, should I hang it
in front of my bed?

36
00:02:34,460 --> 00:02:36,330
Yes, that sounds great.

37
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,830
This is a sunflower.

38
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:43,170
And this is a grape. See that shape?

39
00:02:43,640 --> 00:02:45,170
It's shaped like a grape.

40
00:02:53,950 --> 00:02:56,110
Boss, aren't you heading home?

41
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:58,080
Once I finish this drink.

42
00:02:58,150 --> 00:02:59,150
Go ahead first.

43
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:06,790
Come on. As if I could.

44
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,360
We'll drink together.

45
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:12,930
I was craving some beer anyway.

46
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:19,240
Thank you for earlier.

47
00:03:20,710 --> 00:03:22,870
But wasn't the setup a bit too much?

48
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:26,080
Anyone can see
we have a huge age gap.

49
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,580
Us dating wouldn't make sense.

50
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:30,520
Couples with a big age gap
are the trend these days.

51
00:03:30,580 --> 00:03:31,580
And what?

52
00:03:31,650 --> 00:03:35,250
I run cold,
but now I feel the heat a lot more?

53
00:03:35,490 --> 00:03:39,160
I was stunned
that you could lie so shamelessly.

54
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,690
That wasn't lying.

55
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:42,290
I'm just good at improvising.

56
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:45,600
Besides, when people are dating,

57
00:03:45,660 --> 00:03:47,530
things can always change.

58
00:03:47,530 --> 00:03:49,430
You must have dated a lot.

59
00:03:49,630 --> 00:03:52,900
With this face and body,
isn't it obvious?

60
00:03:55,110 --> 00:03:57,210
Absolutely. Whatever you say.

61
00:03:58,910 --> 00:03:59,910
You were upset earlier, right?

62
00:04:01,150 --> 00:04:02,880
But are they really
your close friends?

63
00:04:03,410 --> 00:04:05,950
They lack basic manners
and have even less tact.

64
00:04:06,780 --> 00:04:09,190
Why do you hang out
with those women?

65
00:04:10,220 --> 00:04:11,420
We're not that close.

66
00:04:11,690 --> 00:04:14,230
We just happened to get acquainted.

67
00:04:15,490 --> 00:04:17,100
Those types
of ambiguous relationships...

68
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,660
are what mess people up.

69
00:04:20,230 --> 00:04:21,430
I saw right through them...

70
00:04:21,500 --> 00:04:24,200
when they said they'd boost sales
but only ordered two cups of coffee.

71
00:04:28,670 --> 00:04:29,670
Thank you.

72
00:04:31,240 --> 00:04:34,050
Well, the setup was a bit absurd,

73
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:37,820
but I appreciated you pretending
to be my boyfriend.

74
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:45,820
Boss, then...

75
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:50,060
Please consider me...

76
00:04:53,870 --> 00:04:55,430
your eternal...

77
00:04:57,540 --> 00:04:58,770
sidekick.

78
00:05:01,670 --> 00:05:02,770
Are you really that thankful?

79
00:05:03,110 --> 00:05:05,080
If you are, how about a bonus?

80
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:06,840
Forget it.

81
00:05:16,890 --> 00:05:18,720
Baby, are they your close friends?

82
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:20,890
Yes.

83
00:05:21,260 --> 00:05:23,800
Then you should have
introduced me to them.

84
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,800
Sorry for the late introduction.

85
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:30,070
I'm Ko Eun Guk, Mi Rae's boyfriend.

86
00:05:31,270 --> 00:05:34,440
He called me his? The nerve...

87
00:05:47,850 --> 00:05:49,920
Did I drink too much coffee today?

88
00:06:02,670 --> 00:06:04,240
(Cheongma)

89
00:06:05,240 --> 00:06:07,610
Did you review the materials
I gave you yesterday...

90
00:06:07,610 --> 00:06:08,770
for the correctional
scholarship program?

91
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,640
Yes, I checked
the Legal Team's review...

92
00:06:10,710 --> 00:06:12,680
and the draft budget.

93
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:17,120
They're likely working
behind the scenes right now...

94
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:19,580
to win over board members
and pass it.

95
00:06:19,980 --> 00:06:23,990
We need to act before they do
and see where the board stands.

96
00:06:24,290 --> 00:06:25,290
Got it.

97
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,590
I will look into
the board members first.

98
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:30,530
This is the list
of the Chairman's people.

99
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:32,330
- Go through it.
- Yes, ma'am.

100
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:35,070
Also,

101
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,300
there's a girl named Ko Eun Seol
on the Design Team.

102
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,410
She's the one whispering
in the Chairman's ear,

103
00:06:42,470 --> 00:06:43,670
and she's a piece of work.

104
00:06:44,210 --> 00:06:47,010
Right now, she's the main person
we need to keep an eye on.

105
00:06:50,680 --> 00:06:52,480
To keep a close eye on her,

106
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:54,250
you'll need to get close
to her first.

107
00:06:55,450 --> 00:06:57,920
She's suspicious by nature.
Are you up for the task?

108
00:07:01,030 --> 00:07:03,090
Yes. I can do it.

109
00:07:04,030 --> 00:07:05,260
If she senses your motive,

110
00:07:05,330 --> 00:07:07,600
she'll go to any lengths
to hide everything.

111
00:07:08,070 --> 00:07:11,940
So don't do anything flashy.
Take your time getting close to her.

112
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,710
The proposal for the hospital store
is very impressive.

113
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:16,870
Who put this together?

114
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:19,610
I did.

115
00:07:20,950 --> 00:07:23,480
I think the details in that proposal
are a bit lacking.

116
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:26,250
The expected effects also seem
to be poorly written.

117
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:28,650
No. This is more than enough.

118
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:32,160
At the proposal stage,
excessive expected effects...

119
00:07:32,220 --> 00:07:34,360
can actually look like
baseless bluffing.

120
00:07:35,130 --> 00:07:36,660
Rather than vague forecasts,

121
00:07:36,730 --> 00:07:38,560
realistic data is more reliable.

122
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:41,430
Good job, Ms. Ko.

123
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:53,810
Ms. Ko, please check the samples
that were rejected...

124
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:55,150
from the factory production line.

125
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:56,810
And bring them all here.

126
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:59,750
Every single one of them?

127
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:01,320
Yes.

128
00:08:01,490 --> 00:08:03,620
Since you are
such a meticulous employee,

129
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:05,720
you should inspect
the defects meticulously too.

130
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:09,460
Isn't visually checking them one by one
the absolute basics?

131
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:13,630
What's wrong?

132
00:08:14,070 --> 00:08:15,200
Is this also too much for you?

133
00:08:16,530 --> 00:08:19,100
Far from it. I'm on it.

134
00:08:21,970 --> 00:08:24,210
You'll have to move them all
before lunch.

135
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:27,680
Wait, is that timeframe too tight?

136
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:31,320
Enjoy your lunch then.

137
00:08:37,520 --> 00:08:38,720
We'll help you.

138
00:08:39,290 --> 00:08:40,520
It's too much to do alone.

139
00:08:41,030 --> 00:08:42,760
Exactly. We'll help.

140
00:08:43,630 --> 00:08:44,730
It's fine.

141
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:48,700
Ms. Kang won't be satisfied
unless I do it all myself.

142
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:53,270
If I get help for no reason,
the backlash will only be worse.

143
00:08:55,410 --> 00:08:57,440
I should just watch
Ko Eun Seol show off like that?

144
00:08:58,610 --> 00:09:00,610
I told you to be prepared
from the start.

145
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:02,810
I told you Ko Eun Seol...

146
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:05,680
would go wild at this company
as soon as she got the job.

147
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,250
She must be incredibly
determined right now.

148
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:10,050
Now that her name's been cleared,

149
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:12,160
she has nothing to fear.

150
00:09:12,890 --> 00:09:13,930
Even so.

151
00:09:14,390 --> 00:09:16,690
Honestly, I didn't expect her
to be this good at her job.

152
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:21,070
Just stay quiet
and watch her calmly for now.

153
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:23,100
How can I do that?

154
00:09:23,170 --> 00:09:25,770
She's even openly flirting
with Seok Jin now.

155
00:09:43,050 --> 00:09:44,790
She's the one whispering
in the Chairman's ear,

156
00:09:44,860 --> 00:09:46,160
and she's a piece of work.

157
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:49,530
Right now, she's the main person
we need to keep an eye on.

158
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,040
Need a hand?

159
00:10:01,410 --> 00:10:03,040
No, I'm good.

160
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:18,660
Hold on a second.

161
00:10:20,990 --> 00:10:24,530
Director Joo's secretary's office
told me to come help you out.

162
00:10:25,230 --> 00:10:27,230
Director Joo's secretary's office?

163
00:10:27,230 --> 00:10:28,430
You know who I mean.

164
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:31,370
The tall and handsome secretary
who was recently hired.

165
00:10:33,170 --> 00:10:34,440
Can I carry these for you?

166
00:10:34,710 --> 00:10:36,710
- I'll take them.
- Sure.

167
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:50,220
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation,
Chairman Kim Jung Sun)

168
00:10:55,730 --> 00:10:57,360
What are you two doing?

169
00:11:13,540 --> 00:11:15,310
Here's the budget for this quarter.

170
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:17,450
Oh, right.

171
00:11:23,250 --> 00:11:24,590
Yesterday...

172
00:11:25,320 --> 00:11:28,030
What were you talking about
with my husband?

173
00:11:29,330 --> 00:11:30,330
Excuse me?

174
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:34,700
You were talking with my husband
in the kitchen yesterday.

175
00:11:35,430 --> 00:11:36,430
Oh, that.

176
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:39,270
He seemed very worried...

177
00:11:39,500 --> 00:11:41,840
that this gathering might have
ruined his relationship...

178
00:11:41,910 --> 00:11:43,810
with Chairman Kim and his wife.

179
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:48,710
And then he got a little agitated.

180
00:11:50,850 --> 00:11:52,180
He got worked up?

181
00:11:57,490 --> 00:11:59,820
That must've caught you off guard.

182
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:02,530
Not at all. It's fine.

183
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:06,000
My husband isn't
that kind of person.

184
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:10,630
As the business expands,
his anxiety seems to grow.

185
00:12:11,870 --> 00:12:14,440
Please be understanding,
Director Joo.

186
00:12:16,040 --> 00:12:18,040
Of course. That I should.

187
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:22,710
Good.

188
00:12:23,410 --> 00:12:24,650
Well, thank you,

189
00:12:25,450 --> 00:12:26,620
Director Joo.

190
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:37,260
(Foundation Chairman's Office)

191
00:12:39,930 --> 00:12:42,900
Of course. I bet the stress
is driving you crazy.

192
00:12:43,770 --> 00:12:46,500
You're getting this anxious
over your husband...

193
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,570
grabbing my wrist?

194
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,180
It's going to be quite a show
from here on out.

195
00:12:52,180 --> 00:12:55,910
Kim Jung Sun, know this.
We're only getting started.

196
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:58,750
(Foundation Chairman's Office)

197
00:13:02,290 --> 00:13:03,450
I'm back.

198
00:13:04,790 --> 00:13:07,290
People would think
you actually have a regular job.

199
00:13:07,560 --> 00:13:09,490
This is all practice.

200
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:13,160
I'm training my body
to handle the commute.

201
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:14,670
Whatever.

202
00:13:15,470 --> 00:13:16,500
Take a look at this.

203
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:18,900
What is it?

204
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:21,610
You know the matchmaker lady...

205
00:13:21,610 --> 00:13:23,540
- at the senior center?
- Sure.

206
00:13:23,910 --> 00:13:25,480
These are the photos she sent.

207
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:27,010
People still do that?

208
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:30,010
Don't people call them
couple managers now?

209
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,720
Stop talking nonsense and look.

210
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:34,490
They are all nice women
with a steady income.

211
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:37,860
Pick one who would make
a good daughter-in-law.

212
00:13:39,090 --> 00:13:41,160
What's the point to this?

213
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:42,190
And Mom,

214
00:13:42,260 --> 00:13:44,760
why would women like this
date Eun Guk?

215
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:46,200
Unbelievable.

216
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:48,600
It's no wonder
the son is struggling,

217
00:13:48,670 --> 00:13:50,730
considering his father
thinks like this.

218
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:53,370
Where does our Eun Guk fall short?

219
00:13:53,770 --> 00:13:56,740
Honestly, Eun Guk is
a bit lacking on paper.

220
00:13:57,040 --> 00:14:00,310
I mean, all he has going for him
are his abs.

221
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:03,480
Besides, is this the time
for him to be dating?

222
00:14:04,050 --> 00:14:08,020
Just you wait.
Your mother has a plan.

223
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:13,060
Hello, Ms. Kang.

224
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:17,460
Are you getting used to the work?

225
00:14:18,430 --> 00:14:19,430
Yes.

226
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:20,860
I'm adjusting to it step by step.

227
00:14:24,500 --> 00:14:27,670
I have a favor to ask you too.
When is a good time for you?

228
00:14:32,040 --> 00:14:34,210
I'm Director Joo's executive secretary.

229
00:14:35,310 --> 00:14:37,650
Regarding your request
for my support,

230
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:40,720
I'll run that by Ms. Joo
and get back to you.

231
00:14:44,020 --> 00:14:45,260
Look here, Secretary Choi,

232
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:48,460
I don't think
you've grasped the situation yet.

233
00:14:49,130 --> 00:14:51,630
Have you not been told who I am yet?

234
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:54,500
I have. You're the CEO's daughter.

235
00:14:54,570 --> 00:14:55,600
And?

236
00:14:56,300 --> 00:14:57,500
Need I say more?

237
00:14:58,540 --> 00:15:00,240
You still need her sign-off?

238
00:15:00,370 --> 00:15:02,140
Yes, I do.

239
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:05,910
I'll run your request for support
by Ms. Joo...

240
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:08,380
and contact you separately.

241
00:15:12,350 --> 00:15:13,480
Then...

242
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:28,600
I see you remembered
the anniversary of Dad's death.

243
00:15:29,830 --> 00:15:30,900
Yes.

244
00:15:31,540 --> 00:15:33,170
I know it's coming up.

245
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:35,140
Are you getting scared again?

246
00:15:40,810 --> 00:15:43,150
Why do you dread
Dad's memorial service every year?

247
00:15:44,150 --> 00:15:47,080
I told you.
Just think of it like a birthday.

248
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:49,650
You're right.

249
00:15:49,890 --> 00:15:52,120
You said it was like
a birthday party.

250
00:15:57,530 --> 00:15:59,860
We prepare Dad's favorite dishes...

251
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,400
and promise to hold onto his memory
for a long, long time.

252
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:04,800
That's what the day is about.

253
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,000
You remember, right?

254
00:16:08,210 --> 00:16:11,040
Yes. I remember, Mr. Seok Jin.

255
00:16:12,310 --> 00:16:14,380
Even though
you're scared of this day,

256
00:16:14,810 --> 00:16:17,720
you make all the dishes
Aunt and Dad liked.

257
00:16:17,780 --> 00:16:19,680
Japchae, tteokguk, and even galbi.

258
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:24,120
That's right. I'm good at cooking.

259
00:16:26,690 --> 00:16:28,790
Cook up all those tasty dishes
this time too.

260
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:30,530
Okay?

261
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:33,260
Okay.

262
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:51,980
I made a lunch appointment
with Chairman Kim.

263
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:56,350
Oh, really? That's great. When?

264
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:00,420
I don't think you need to go.

265
00:17:00,920 --> 00:17:05,000
We agreed it'd be just me,
Chairman Kim, and his wife.

266
00:17:06,860 --> 00:17:10,070
If it's just the three of you,
shouldn't I tag along too?

267
00:17:10,270 --> 00:17:11,570
You know how it is.

268
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:14,300
My father was especially fond
of Chairman Kim.

269
00:17:14,710 --> 00:17:18,710
I'm going to this meal looking at it
as meeting my father's friend.

270
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:21,580
Rather than talking business,

271
00:17:21,650 --> 00:17:24,080
we're just going to reminisce
about my late parents...

272
00:17:24,150 --> 00:17:26,050
and have a comfortable meal.

273
00:17:29,650 --> 00:17:31,420
You get what I'm saying, right?

274
00:17:32,620 --> 00:17:34,390
Sure, do whatever you want.

275
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:40,400
Goodness.

276
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:48,110
Come in.

277
00:17:57,310 --> 00:17:59,580
It's a supplement to help you sleep.

278
00:18:03,550 --> 00:18:04,590
Thank you.

279
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:08,160
Sir.

280
00:18:09,430 --> 00:18:13,900
Should I look into Chairman Kim
a bit more?

281
00:18:15,570 --> 00:18:18,470
You want to look into Chairman Kim?

282
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:20,100
Yes.

283
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:21,740
He's the head...

284
00:18:21,810 --> 00:18:24,710
of the Metropolitan Distribution
Network Development Council.

285
00:18:25,680 --> 00:18:27,780
If we get on his bad side,

286
00:18:28,710 --> 00:18:31,180
Cheongma will suffer massive losses.

287
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:32,680
So,

288
00:18:33,650 --> 00:18:38,420
you want to dig into his background
and secure some leverage in advance.

289
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,760
Is that it?

290
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:41,860
If possible, yes.

291
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:43,860
All right.

292
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:48,870
From what I know, Chairman Kim
isn't exactly clean either.

293
00:18:48,930 --> 00:18:51,170
He definitely has
some dirty secrets.

294
00:18:52,070 --> 00:18:53,600
No matter how friendly we are,

295
00:18:54,170 --> 00:18:56,570
relationships alone
are not enough to win.

296
00:18:59,040 --> 00:19:01,580
Can you handle this quietly?

297
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:03,580
Of course.

298
00:19:04,180 --> 00:19:06,450
If it's for you and Cheongma,

299
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:08,050
I'll do whatever it takes.

300
00:19:09,650 --> 00:19:10,820
Thank you, Director Joo.

301
00:19:12,490 --> 00:19:13,620
I'm counting on you.

302
00:19:48,860 --> 00:19:50,030
(Incoming Call)

303
00:20:16,520 --> 00:20:21,220
(Incoming Call)

304
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:37,210
Hello? Yes.

305
00:20:38,540 --> 00:20:40,380
That corporate investment.

306
00:20:40,780 --> 00:20:43,410
We agreed to offset the cost
with proceeds from the artwork.

307
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:49,820
I already took care of
all the approval documents myself.

308
00:20:50,020 --> 00:20:54,490
Just hurry up and buy
the ancestral family land. Got it?

309
00:20:55,660 --> 00:20:57,930
Before the auditors catch on,

310
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,230
we need to get the contract
signed and sealed by this week.

311
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,300
Understood?

312
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:42,170
Chairman Kim's wife held
an exhibition two months ago.

313
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:44,910
Find out the purchase prices
of the paintings and the buyers.

314
00:21:45,810 --> 00:21:48,080
I'll look into it and report back.

315
00:21:58,590 --> 00:21:59,990
Hello, Ms. Joo.

316
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:05,030
She's even openly flirting
with Seok Jin now.

317
00:22:06,630 --> 00:22:07,660
Eun Seol.

318
00:22:14,270 --> 00:22:16,370
I bet you haven't had lunch yet.

319
00:22:17,110 --> 00:22:18,110
That's right.

320
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:20,280
Care to join me?

321
00:22:21,410 --> 00:22:22,450
I'd love to.

322
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,550
Come to think of it,

323
00:22:27,750 --> 00:22:29,020
I think this is the first time...

324
00:22:29,090 --> 00:22:31,290
it's just the two of us
eating together.

325
00:22:32,620 --> 00:22:33,920
Yes, it is.

326
00:22:36,060 --> 00:22:37,930
I said I'd look after you,

327
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:40,030
so I'm sorry
I haven't been more attentive.

328
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:43,100
Please don't say that. It's fine.

329
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:45,800
Just having
my mother's friend around...

330
00:22:45,870 --> 00:22:47,440
gives me so much strength.

331
00:22:48,110 --> 00:22:50,410
Thank you for thinking that way.

332
00:22:52,510 --> 00:22:56,150
You're so radiant
and pretty, Eun Seol.

333
00:22:56,910 --> 00:22:58,180
Aren't you seeing anyone?

334
00:22:59,620 --> 00:23:00,620
Excuse me?

335
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:03,520
Your life has settled down
to a degree,

336
00:23:04,190 --> 00:23:06,160
and you're in the prime
of your life.

337
00:23:06,890 --> 00:23:08,730
You should definitely be dating.

338
00:23:10,730 --> 00:23:11,730
Right.

339
00:23:13,230 --> 00:23:16,170
Is there somebody you like?

340
00:23:17,430 --> 00:23:19,240
Yes, I think there is.

341
00:23:28,040 --> 00:23:29,810
Is it Chief Cha by any chance?

342
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,990
Is it really?

343
00:23:36,820 --> 00:23:39,320
No, of course not. Not at all.

344
00:23:40,860 --> 00:23:41,930
But...

345
00:23:42,860 --> 00:23:43,960
But why...

346
00:23:44,490 --> 00:23:47,830
Why did you think I like Chief Cha?

347
00:23:48,030 --> 00:23:49,830
I was just asking.

348
00:23:50,300 --> 00:23:52,170
He's your boss, after all.

349
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:54,810
Honestly, even to me,

350
00:23:54,870 --> 00:23:56,810
Chief Cha is quite
an attractive man.

351
00:23:58,540 --> 00:24:00,080
It's nothing like that.

352
00:24:01,280 --> 00:24:02,280
Right?

353
00:24:03,450 --> 00:24:07,450
No matter how handsome he is,
Chief Cha is already taken.

354
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:10,990
My friend Hee Jung's daughter...

355
00:24:11,050 --> 00:24:13,320
would never go for a guy
with a fiancee.

356
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:17,130
Yes, of course.

357
00:24:17,660 --> 00:24:19,830
My silly joke is going
to give you indigestion.

358
00:24:20,930 --> 00:24:22,170
Go ahead and eat.

359
00:24:23,030 --> 00:24:24,030
Sure.

360
00:24:37,610 --> 00:24:40,050
Chief Cha is already taken.

361
00:24:41,320 --> 00:24:42,920
My friend Hee Jung's daughter...

362
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,920
would never go for a guy
with a fiancee.

363
00:25:21,320 --> 00:25:22,860
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

364
00:25:28,030 --> 00:25:30,270
You put your ring back on.

365
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:32,040
What?

366
00:25:33,970 --> 00:25:34,970
Oh, this.

367
00:25:36,140 --> 00:25:38,380
I had to report
to the CEO this morning.

368
00:25:38,880 --> 00:25:40,540
He always pays close attention.

369
00:25:46,350 --> 00:25:48,420
Then you shouldn't take it off.

370
00:25:50,990 --> 00:25:51,990
What?

371
00:25:52,160 --> 00:25:54,020
If you keep taking it on and off,

372
00:25:54,290 --> 00:25:56,330
won't you end up losing
the CEO's trust?

373
00:25:58,260 --> 00:26:01,800
More than anyone,
you need to stay on his good side.

374
00:26:03,830 --> 00:26:04,830
You're right.

375
00:26:05,900 --> 00:26:08,670
I want to achieve solid results
with the brand I launched,

376
00:26:09,310 --> 00:26:11,140
and have it recognized
as Cheongma's core business.

377
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:20,180
I'm rooting for you, Seok Jin.

378
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:23,120
I mean, Chief Cha.

379
00:26:25,620 --> 00:26:26,620
Thanks.

380
00:26:28,730 --> 00:26:29,790
Well then...

381
00:26:30,490 --> 00:26:32,530
I'll revise the proposal
and submit it again,

382
00:26:33,100 --> 00:26:34,100
Chief.

383
00:26:58,020 --> 00:26:59,860
- Welcome.
- Welcome.

384
00:27:00,890 --> 00:27:02,790
Is there a Ko Eun Guk here?

385
00:27:02,990 --> 00:27:04,530
Yes, that's me.

386
00:27:05,500 --> 00:27:07,730
I was told I could find you here.

387
00:27:07,730 --> 00:27:08,800
What?

388
00:27:17,870 --> 00:27:20,280
I see. My grandmother set this up.

389
00:27:21,010 --> 00:27:23,180
Didn't you know
about our blind date today?

390
00:27:24,080 --> 00:27:25,980
No, I had no idea.

391
00:27:26,620 --> 00:27:27,650
I'm sorry.

392
00:27:30,690 --> 00:27:33,760
The thing is, I'm really not in
a great place in life to date.

393
00:27:34,420 --> 00:27:35,490
What?

394
00:27:35,860 --> 00:27:37,290
My situation right now is a bit...

395
00:27:40,530 --> 00:27:42,130
Careful. Are you hurt?

396
00:27:42,130 --> 00:27:43,500
Gosh, I am fine.

397
00:27:44,170 --> 00:27:45,770
Don't worry about me
and go back over there.

398
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:47,970
Just hold still for a second.

399
00:27:53,080 --> 00:27:54,410
Are you okay?

400
00:27:54,680 --> 00:27:56,080
This looks like
it's going to blister.

401
00:27:56,150 --> 00:27:58,620
I'm fine. Really, I'm fine.

402
00:27:58,820 --> 00:28:00,580
How are you fine? It's all red.

403
00:28:00,650 --> 00:28:02,420
It's fine, I mean...

404
00:28:03,420 --> 00:28:04,720
Just keep it on there.

405
00:28:06,490 --> 00:28:08,290
See? I told you I'm fine.

406
00:28:09,690 --> 00:28:11,430
What? Did she leave?

407
00:28:11,860 --> 00:28:13,030
I would have left too.

408
00:28:13,560 --> 00:28:15,600
Why would you fuss over me
when you're on a date?

409
00:28:15,600 --> 00:28:17,600
It's your fault for making me worry.

410
00:28:18,300 --> 00:28:19,840
Why did you have to get hurt?

411
00:28:20,140 --> 00:28:21,140
Seriously.

412
00:28:28,310 --> 00:28:32,050
So companies wanting
to enter the mall...

413
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:36,750
bought
Chairman Kim's wife's artwork...

414
00:28:36,750 --> 00:28:37,950
at several times its value?

415
00:28:38,790 --> 00:28:39,860
Yes.

416
00:28:40,390 --> 00:28:41,690
Plus, since he holds...

417
00:28:41,690 --> 00:28:43,430
the development rights
for the outlet,

418
00:28:43,860 --> 00:28:46,560
he's buying up the surrounding land
for pennies on the dollar.

419
00:28:47,430 --> 00:28:48,570
Do we have solid evidence?

420
00:28:49,130 --> 00:28:50,300
Chairman Kim's wife is holding...

421
00:28:50,300 --> 00:28:52,000
another solo exhibition
in a few days.

422
00:28:52,800 --> 00:28:54,700
The businesses looking
to open stores at the outlet...

423
00:28:54,970 --> 00:28:58,480
are already
on the gallery's VIP list.

424
00:28:59,240 --> 00:29:00,380
Is that so?

425
00:29:01,010 --> 00:29:03,350
If we dig into that,
we should be able to find...

426
00:29:03,410 --> 00:29:04,650
the source of the stench.

427
00:29:06,420 --> 00:29:07,650
Good work, Director Joo.

428
00:29:12,460 --> 00:29:14,590
This will be quite a sight.

429
00:29:15,790 --> 00:29:19,530
He called me a mere merchant
with no class,

430
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:21,700
yet he's the one
who smells of corruption.

431
00:29:23,870 --> 00:29:26,440
I'll track Chairman Kim's movements
and report back to you.

432
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:29,310
Yes, please do.

433
00:29:33,510 --> 00:29:37,680
By the way, sir,
you don't even smoke,

434
00:29:38,210 --> 00:29:40,680
but you seem
to really cherish that lighter.

435
00:29:40,750 --> 00:29:42,020
Oh, this?

436
00:29:43,490 --> 00:29:44,750
It was my father's.

437
00:29:46,220 --> 00:29:47,720
No matter how tough things got,

438
00:29:48,360 --> 00:29:50,960
my father insisted on using
a nice lighter.

439
00:29:52,260 --> 00:29:54,100
I lost it decades ago,

440
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:57,570
but I asked around and managed
to find the exact same model.

441
00:29:58,570 --> 00:30:00,800
Whenever things are not going well
or I feel frustrated,

442
00:30:01,870 --> 00:30:03,210
fiddling with it like this...

443
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:05,840
makes me feel much better.

444
00:30:07,740 --> 00:30:09,550
I had no idea it held such meaning.

445
00:30:10,310 --> 00:30:12,250
Anyway, thanks to you,

446
00:30:12,750 --> 00:30:14,650
it looks like things were resolved
with ease.

447
00:30:16,620 --> 00:30:19,320
I can finally breathe a little.

448
00:30:25,860 --> 00:30:29,130
So you're saying
a retrial won't be easy?

449
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:33,400
The law is actually...

450
00:30:33,470 --> 00:30:35,440
much more conservative
than you might think.

451
00:30:36,510 --> 00:30:37,940
I'm not saying it's a lost cause,

452
00:30:38,580 --> 00:30:40,040
but we're in for a long battle.

453
00:30:41,210 --> 00:30:43,910
Since the real culprit is dead,
it makes things even harder.

454
00:30:45,720 --> 00:30:46,720
I see.

455
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,220
It's not like we're completely
out of options.

456
00:30:50,550 --> 00:30:53,920
Death doesn't mean
the truth gets buried with them.

457
00:30:55,160 --> 00:30:56,730
If we dig deeper
into Manager Na's life,

458
00:30:56,790 --> 00:30:58,900
other evidence will surface.

459
00:31:03,570 --> 00:31:06,470
Hey, don't tell me
you're losing heart already.

460
00:31:08,170 --> 00:31:11,070
Stay positive, okay?
We still have a long way to go.

461
00:31:11,570 --> 00:31:13,680
We need to gather our strength
and keep pushing forward together.

462
00:31:15,280 --> 00:31:16,750
Just trust me, okay?

463
00:31:18,780 --> 00:31:20,620
Yes, I will.

464
00:31:21,720 --> 00:31:23,120
Thank you, Attorney Seo.

465
00:31:34,360 --> 00:31:35,670
I told you.

466
00:31:36,070 --> 00:31:38,370
Just think of Dad's memorial service
like a birthday.

467
00:31:39,540 --> 00:31:40,570
That's right.

468
00:31:41,070 --> 00:31:43,010
He said it's like a birthday party.

469
00:31:44,810 --> 00:31:47,040
I'm going to make
tons of the dishes...

470
00:31:47,110 --> 00:31:50,350
my sweet husband loved
and set the table for him.

471
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:16,100
(A Trap Called Desire)

472
00:33:17,100 --> 00:33:18,770
If we act rashly right now,

473
00:33:18,840 --> 00:33:20,370
they will just cut their losses
and run.

474
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:23,410
I suppose it's time
for me to make a move.

475
00:33:23,470 --> 00:33:25,710
I feel like I open up
so easily around you.

476
00:33:25,710 --> 00:33:28,140
Sometimes a casual relationship
is just easier.

477
00:33:28,140 --> 00:33:29,780
Who knows? It could grow deeper.

478
00:33:30,210 --> 00:33:31,850
Why are you being so twisted?

479
00:33:31,910 --> 00:33:35,280
I went and apologized on your behalf
for the mess you made.

480
00:33:35,350 --> 00:33:37,150
Did you really not know
today was my dad's memorial service?

481
00:33:37,220 --> 00:33:39,620
On the CEO's desk,
there was a lighter.

482
00:33:39,690 --> 00:33:41,920
I saw an identical one at my house.

483
00:33:41,990 --> 00:33:44,060
I just happened
to get a little muddy,

484
00:33:44,130 --> 00:33:46,430
and I'm currently
wiping away the dirt.

485
00:33:46,760 --> 00:33:47,930
That's my take on it.

486
00:33:48,970 --> 00:33:50,930
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
